# #5833, C7. The cold load's read and its load are separate steps: a re-claim (the
# re-created incarnation's first initialisation) raises the entry between them, and the
# load then sets it back to the lower value it read, so a straddler under the purged
# generation is admitted above L's recorded close.
MODULE: StraddlerBelowInitColdLoadLowersLoadedGeneration
TARGET: StraddlerBelowInit
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a late cold load lowers a generation a re-claim raised
PERTURBS: ColdLoadApply

--- FIND
    /\ loaded' = [loaded EXCEPT ![i] = Max2(@, Max2(rd[i], walFloor[i] + 1))]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the load overwrites, never max-merges.
    /\ loaded' = [loaded EXCEPT ![i] = Max2(rd[i], walFloor[i] + 1)]
--- END
